      "recentReviews": [
        {
          "text": "This is University of Greenwich.\nA wonderful place for walks and photos. As a student of this university, I truly appreciate the huge open space that creates a peaceful atmosphere. The classic architectural style of the buildings is both solemn and beautifully timeless. It's perfect for a quiet stroll, enjoying the grandeur and elegance all around.",
          "time": 1750707486830,
          "rating": 5,
          "authorName": "mohd mudaser mastan khan"
        },
        {
          "text": "The University of Greenwich campus is stunning, beautifully blending historic architecture with lush green spaces. Every corner offers picturesque views that make studying and relaxing here truly inspiring. It's a peaceful and visually captivating environment that enhances the whole university experience.",
          "time": 1749116276268,
          "rating": 5,
          "authorName": "Mohammed Iqbal"
        },
        {
          "text": "The school is in an amazing locations. Greenwich feels like a small town but has all the amenities of a city and easy access to central London. The school itself is beautiful. I never complain about going to school because I'm always just excited to look at the scenery. The teachers are nice, the staff are helpful, and I'm very glad I chose this as my school!",
          "time": 1770680408916,
          "rating": 5,
          "authorName": "Anne Malone"
        },
        {
          "text": "I went to this amazing university for an open day, which included the Old Navy College. The vistas are stunning.\n\nI genuinely value how the old structures have been conserved to show off their previous splendor and to be enjoyed by future generations. A pleasant stroll along the Thames River.",
          "time": 1744887746450,
          "rating": 5,
          "authorName": "Babji Vundavilli"
        },
        {
          "text": "We came to visit this remarkable university 2 days after Christmas, and some of the facilities were still closed. The Old Navy College was a part of it, and we took a lot of photos within the surrounding area.\n\nAs an architect, I truly appreciate how the historical buildings had been preserved, to reflect their former grandeur, and for the future generations to experience.\n\nWe visited the famous Queen's House, where the late Queen Elizabeth II regularly visited during her lifetime.",
          "time": 1705156025217,
          "rating": 5,
          "authorName": "Sazali M Salleh"
        }
      ],
